I replied on Otto's comment with this evidence and resolved it.

**New Low finding (margin 01M2K0045A5SEZAKMB1KZAKVXS, `mentionSlugs.ts:15`).** A fence must now start its line, so two kinds of fence stop being treated as code:
- A fence inside a quote: `"> ```\n> @x\n> ```\n@y"` gives `["x","y"]`.
- A fence at the start of a list item: `"- ```\n  @x\n  ```\n@y"` gives `["x","y"]`.

The commit before ae791125 gave `["y"]` for both. So a mention inside a quoted code block now starts an agent.

The fix I suggested lets quote markers and list markers come before each fence: ``p = ^(?:[ \t]*(?:>|[-*+]|\d+[.)]))*[ \t]{0,3}``. On both inputs above it gives `["y"]`. The other cases I ran did not change.

I did not run the test suite. I ran only the function, from the commit, in a temporary folder.

